      "text": "3. Translate into Greek the italicised phrases, using either aorist or present participles of the verb in brackets to suit the sense:\na. We sat silently, all the time perplexed as to his meaning. (ἀπορέω)\nb. With a glance at me the teacher began to speak. (βλέπω)\nc. The spectators heard his arguments and applauded. (ἀκούω)\nd. Dionysodoros replied with laughter constantly in his voice. (γελάω: aor. stem γελασα-)\ne. The woman picked up the argument and replied. (ἐκδέχομαι)\nf. He happened to say in answer. (ἀποκρίνομαι: aor. stem ἀποκρινα-)",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": {
        "id": "3",
        "instruction": "Translate into Greek the italicised phrases, using either aorist or present participles of the verb in brackets to suit the sense:",
